      <div class="container two-col">
        <div class="prose">
          <h2>Free collection, any condition</h2>
          <p>It doesn't matter what state the car is in — running or not, damaged, rusted through, failed its last MOT, or simply sat on the drive unused for years. If it's ready to go, we'll collect it, and there's no charge for the collection itself. This covers cars of any make and model across <a href="../areas/birmingham.html">Birmingham</a> and the wider West Midlands.</p>

          <h2>How it works</h2>
          <p>Call or WhatsApp us with the vehicle's make and model, its location, and roughly what condition it's in — whether it starts and moves under its own power, or needs to be loaded. We'll arrange a collection time, and where possible we can often collect the same day, depending on your area and how busy we are. Have the keys ready, along with the vehicle's log book (V5C) if you can find it, since that helps the process go smoothly.</p>

          <ul class="checklist">
            <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg> Non-runners and cars that won't start.</li>
            <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg> Cars that have failed their MOT.</li>
            <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg> Accident-damaged vehicles no longer worth repairing.</li>
            <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg> Old cars that have sat unused on a driveway or in a garage for years.</li>
            <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg> Any make or model — we don't turn cars away for being too old, too rusty or too far gone.</li>
          </ul>

          <h2>Where your car goes</h2>
          <!-- CONFIRM WITH ABDUL: are we an ATF ourselves, or do we collect and hand off to a licensed ATF partner? Copy must match whichever is true, including any wording about DVLA notification or issuing a Certificate of Destruction. Do not publish specific legal claims until this is confirmed. -->
          <p>Once collected, your vehicle is taken on to be dealt with properly and in line with the relevant regulations for end-of-life vehicles. If you need documentation or more detail for your own records, ask us when you book collection and we'll confirm exactly what applies to your vehicle.</p>

          <div class="callout">
            <p><strong>Before we collect.</strong> Please remove any personal belongings from the car beforehand if you're able to — we can't be responsible for anything left inside once it's collected. If you have the V5C log book, having it ready speeds things up, but let us know if you can't locate it and we'll talk through the options.</p>
          </div>

          <h2>Not sure this is the right service?</h2>
          <p>If your car has broken down and you need it recovered rather than scrapped, our <a href="breakdown-recovery-birmingham.html">breakdown recovery</a> or general <a href="car-recovery-birmingham.html">car recovery</a> pages cover that. If you're planning a non-emergency move of a car that still has some life in it — to storage, a new owner, or another address — see <a href="car-transport-birmingham.html">car transport</a> instead.</p>
        </div>

